   "he": "וְטוֹבְלָן בִּמְקוֹמָן: וְהָאִיכָּא חֲצִיצָה!",
   "en": "And we learned in our mishna: If the animals’ chains became ritually impure, «one may immerse them while they are in their place» on the animal, and they need not first be removed. The Gemara raises a question: «Isn’t this an obstruction» that renders the immersion invalid? The rings of the chain are firmly attached to the chain, and there is no room for the water of the ritual bath to completely surround the chain."
